WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.530
- [Instructor] What we're
going to do in this video

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:05.290
is think about different ways
to represent multiplication.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.700
And especially connect it to the notions

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.460
of skip counting and the number line.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:15.460
So if we were to think about
what four times two means,

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.820
we've already seen in other videos,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.200
you could view this as four groups of two.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.000
So we could have four groups,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.670
so one group, two groups,

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.810
three groups, and four groups,

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.160
and each of them have two of something.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.870
I'll just put two little circles here.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.220
So you have two there,

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.540
you have two there,

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.320
you have two there,

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.770
and you have two there,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.440
and you could also view that

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.220
as four twos, or four twos added together.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.260
So we could view it as two plus two

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.530
plus two plus two.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:50.510
And this, of course, is going
to be two plus two is four,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.040
four plus two is six,
six plus two is eight.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.560
We see that over here,

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.770
we could even skip count.

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.380
Two, four, six, eight.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.500
Four times two is equal to eight.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.380
We can also think about
that on a number line.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:05.940
So I'm gonna make a little
bit of a number line here.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.940
And so we could imagine four
times two being, all right.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.940
So this is one times two,

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.810
two times two,

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.560
three times two,

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.530
and four times two.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:21.880
So we started at zero,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.250
and we took four hops of
two along the number line

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.910
to end up at eight.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:32.650
We went from zero to
two, four, six, eight.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.000
We just skip counted our way to eight.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.610
So if I were to ask a
similar question, actually,

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.530
let me draw a little series of hops,

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.900
and I want you to think
about it the other way.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.030
What multiplication does that represent?

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.350
So let's say I start here

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.530
and then I'm going to hop like this.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.240
So I'm gonna go there

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.020
and then I'm gonna go there.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.030
I'm taking equal jumps every time.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.300
Then I'm gonna go there.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.539
Then I'm gonna go there.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:06.250
Then I'm going to go over there.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.130
So what would that represent,

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.630
if we used the same type of ideas

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.210
that we just thought about?

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:16.210
Well I went from zero to
four, eight, 12, 16, 20.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.360
I'm skip counting by four.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:22.120
So you could imagine this is
probably something times four.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.450
Now how many hops did I take?

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.350
I took one, two, three,
four, five hops of four.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.820
So this is five times four.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:34.340
And we can see that we ended up at 20.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.360
We could also view this
as being the same thing

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.360
as five fours or four plus four plus four

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.920
plus four plus four, and
you see that over here.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.110
You have, we're starting
at zero, we're adding four,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.060
then another four, then another four,

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.470
then another four, and another four.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.690
We have five fours here.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.490
Let's do one more.

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.010
So I'm gonna have a number line here

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.440
and think about what it would mean

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:04.440
to say, do something like
seven times three, times three.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:12.270
Well, we could view that
as seven hops of three

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.520
starting at zero, seven equal hops.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.900
So one,

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.290
two,

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.430
three,

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.290
four,

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.990
five,

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.890
six, and seven.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:29.500
We end up at 21, so this is equal to 21.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.910
You could also view this
as we took seven threes

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:34.210
and added them together.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.890
And you could also view
it as skip counting.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.919
You went from zero to
three, six, nine, 12,

00:03:38.919 --> 00:03:41.030
15, 18, and 21.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.270
Now just out of interest,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.920
what if we went the other way around?

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.410
What if we were to take
three hops of seven?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.763
What would that be?

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.210
Well, we would start here

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.080
and so we would take our first hop

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.790
of seven right over there.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.640
Get to seven, then if we
take another hop of seven,

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.840
we get to 14,

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.940
and then if we take another hop of seven,

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.670
we get to 21, interesting.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.280
At least for this situation,

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.320
whether we took seven hops of three

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.910
or three hops of seven, we
got to the exact same value.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.530
I encourage you to think about
whether that's always going

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.000
to be the case.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.843
I'll see you in a future video.

